---
import { Icon } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
---

<section class="value" aria-labelledby="value-title">
  <div class="value-heading">
    <p>Why Arcantry</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="value-title">Compose what the project already knows</h2>
      <p>Arcantry discovers versioned knowledge sources independently, then lets you choose which ones to observe, validate, or manage.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="value-grid">
    <article>
      <Icon name="approve-check-circle" />
      <h3>Observe without a footprint</h3>
      <p>Inspect an empty or mature project without requiring Git, configuration, or project tooling.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <Icon name="puzzle" />
      <h3>Keep responsibilities distinct</h3>
      <p>OpenSpec, changelogs, todo.txt queues, and skills retain separate roles and versions.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <Icon name="approve-check" />
      <h3>Change through explicit plans</h3>
      <p>Preview source transitions, verify their inputs, and apply only an unchanged plan.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="comparison" aria-labelledby="comparison-title">
  <div class="comparison-heading">
    <p>With and without</p>
    <h2 id="comparison-title">Make project knowledge inspectable without flattening it</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="comparison-table-shell">
    <table class="comparison-flow">
      <colgroup>
        <col class="comparison-area-column" />
        <col />
        <col />
      </colgroup>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Area</th>
          <th class="comparison-before-heading" scope="col">Without Arcantry</th>
          <th class="comparison-after-heading" scope="col">With Arcantry</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><span>01</span><h3>Discovery</h3></th>
          <td class="comparison-before"><p>Each tool must rediscover files, conventions, and missing sources.</p></td>
          <td class="comparison-after"><p>One inspection describes the sources that exist and the ones that do not.</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><span>02</span><h3>Ownership</h3></th>
          <td class="comparison-before"><p>Authority, projections, queues, and procedures are easy to treat as one layer.</p></td>
          <td class="comparison-after"><p>Each source declares its role, management level, visibility, and adapter.</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><span>03</span><h3>Structural change</h3></th>
          <td class="comparison-before"><p>A migration can mix discovery, decisions, and file writes in one step.</p></td>
          <td class="comparison-after"><p><code>repo plan</code> records hashes and <code>repo apply</code> rejects drift before writing.</p></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="contract-map" aria-labelledby="contract-title">
  <div class="contract-heading">
    <p>Explore Arcantry</p>
    <h2 id="contract-title">Choose the part of the stack you need</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="contract-lanes">
    <a class="local-lane" href="/arcantry/reference/repository-contract/#roles-in-the-stack">
      <div class="lane-title"><Icon name="database" /><span>Project knowledge stack</span></div>
      <h3>Give each source one clear role</h3>
      <p>See how authority, projections, queues, capabilities, privacy, and integrity evidence fit together.</p>
      <span class="lane-action">Understand the stack <Icon name="right-arrow" /></span>
    </a>
    <ol class="product-lane">
      <li><a href="/arcantry/getting-started/"><Icon name="approve-check-circle" /><span><strong>Inspect a project</strong><small>Run the CLI without changing the target directory</small></span><Icon name="right-arrow" /></a></li>
      <li><a href="/arcantry/adoption/#choose-an-adoption-path"><Icon name="code-branch" /><span><strong>Choose an adoption path</strong><small>Stay trace-free or add external or tracked configuration</small></span><Icon name="right-arrow" /></a></li>
      <li><a href="/arcantry/guides/todo-txt/"><Icon name="document" /><span><strong>Use a short queue</strong><small>Preview shared or private todo.txt changes</small></span><Icon name="right-arrow" /></a></li>
      <li><a href="/arcantry/skills/#choose-a-distribution-path"><Icon name="puzzle" /><span><strong>Choose a skill</strong><small>Link one workflow or install the full catalog</small></span><Icon name="right-arrow" /></a></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="journey" id="quickstart" aria-labelledby="quickstart-title">
  <div class="journey-heading">
    <p>Three adoption decisions</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="quickstart-title">Start with observation, then add only what helps</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ol class="journey-steps">
    <li>
      <span class="step-icon"><Icon name="approve-check-circle" /></span>
      <div><span>01</span><h3>Stay trace-free</h3><p>Discover supported sources and compatibility without creating configuration or project files.</p><div class="step-command"><span>$</span><code>arcantry repo inspect</code></div></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-icon"><Icon name="puzzle" /></span>
      <div><span>02</span><h3>Add configuration where it belongs</h3><p>Keep it outside the project or track one <code>arcantry.toml</code> when responsibilities must be explicit.</p><div class="step-command"><span>$</span><code>arcantry <b>--cwd</b> . <b>--config</b> ../arcantry.toml repo inspect</code></div></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-icon"><Icon name="approve-check" /></span>
      <div><span>03</span><h3>Use one capability by itself</h3><p>Queues and skills remain useful even when the project adopts no other Arcantry source.</p><div class="step-command"><span>$</span><code>arcantry skills list</code></div></div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
  <div class="proof-heading">
    <p>Expected result</p>
    <h2 id="proof-title">A stack that preserves the project's existing boundaries</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="proof-stage">
    <article class="proof-feature">
      <span class="proof-index">01</span>
      <Icon name="approve-check" />
      <div><h3>No project shape is required</h3><p>An empty directory, a non-Git project, or a mature monorepo can be inspected before any adoption decision.</p></div>
    </article>
    <div class="proof-stack">
      <article>
        <span class="proof-index">02</span>
        <Icon name="database" />
        <div><h3>Meaning stays with its source</h3><p>Managed changelog prose comes from OpenSpec, while observed changelogs and independent queues remain valid.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="proof-index">03</span>
        <Icon name="code-branch" />
        <div><h3>Changed inputs stop the apply</h3><p>Plans record expected hashes, and application verifies them before committing file operations.</p></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
